1
00:00:00,126 --> 00:00:02,795
It didn't work out for us as a couple,

2
00:00:02,878 --> 00:00:06,132
but he's the best person I know.

3
00:00:06,507 --> 00:00:09,176
The way he kicked Uncle Teddy out…

4
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:11,345
It's like he's having fun with it.

5
00:00:11,637 --> 00:00:13,556
You know that I love you so much, right?

6
00:00:13,639 --> 00:00:17,393
I'm not at the point of marriage yet.

7
00:00:17,476 --> 00:00:20,479
Diana, if we don't feel the same way,

8
00:00:20,563 --> 00:00:22,732
then I won't force this. I'll just leave.

9
00:00:22,815 --> 00:00:24,942
I've never felt this way before.

10
00:00:25,985 --> 00:00:27,069
What's this nonsense?

11
00:00:27,903 --> 00:00:28,904
This is a family matter.

12
00:00:29,238 --> 00:00:30,740
Who do you think you are?

13
00:00:31,198 --> 00:00:32,283
Let go of my husband.

14
00:00:35,411 --> 00:00:36,704
We're married.

15
00:00:40,082 --> 00:00:41,876
-Boss.
-Did you find anything?

16
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:46,714
As we all know, Cecilia Pineda
is a former La Familia employee.

17
00:00:47,506 --> 00:00:49,383
She was a suspect in the factory fire.

18
00:00:49,675 --> 00:00:50,801
She had a family.

19
00:00:50,885 --> 00:00:52,678
She raised her two kids on her own.

20
00:00:53,429 --> 00:00:55,306
I found her children as well.

21
00:00:55,389 --> 00:00:57,266
They're professionals now.

22
00:00:58,684 --> 00:01:00,311
They have families of their own too.

23
00:01:00,394 --> 00:01:03,606
But what's her connection to Ricardo?
Why does he visit her grave?

24
00:01:04,023 --> 00:01:07,693
I also found out that Cecilia got pregnant
when she was just a teenager.

25
00:01:08,027 --> 00:01:09,403
But she was no longer with the kid.

26
00:01:09,904 --> 00:01:10,780
Where is he then?

27
00:01:11,322 --> 00:01:12,490
The father took him in.

28
00:01:12,573 --> 00:01:14,325
Based from what I've gathered,

29
00:01:14,408 --> 00:01:15,910
he was taken to another country.

30
00:01:16,368 --> 00:01:18,454
-Where?
-To Indonesia.

31
00:01:20,706 --> 00:01:21,957
That's where Ricardo's from.

32
00:01:22,041 --> 00:01:25,085
This is the birth certificate
of Cecilia's first born.

33
00:01:25,169 --> 00:01:29,340
And here is the birth certificate
that I got back then

34
00:01:29,423 --> 00:01:31,425
when you first had me investigate Ricardo.

35
00:01:31,509 --> 00:01:33,219
The details are the exact same.

36
00:01:34,094 --> 00:01:36,138
Same date and place of birth.

37
00:01:37,598 --> 00:01:38,808
So is the age, but…

38
00:01:38,891 --> 00:01:40,392
the mother's name
and surname are different.

39
00:01:40,476 --> 00:01:42,937
I'm guessing that he's using
a fake birth certificate

40
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:44,104
to leave the country.

41
00:01:44,188 --> 00:01:45,856
He's Cecilia's son.

42
00:01:48,359 --> 00:01:50,194
My hunch is right.

43
00:01:51,862 --> 00:01:53,489
He planned all of this.

44
00:01:54,573 --> 00:01:55,950
Ricardo was the one behind all of it!

45
00:03:04,059 --> 00:03:06,979
Sis, please answer the phone. Please…

46
00:03:12,109 --> 00:03:14,445
Come on, come--

47
00:03:18,782 --> 00:03:21,327
-Dad?
-Hello, Georgia.

48
00:03:21,410 --> 00:03:23,454
Is your Auntie Diana in her office?

49
00:03:23,787 --> 00:03:25,331
She's not here, Dad.

50
00:03:27,124 --> 00:03:29,293
If you see her, tell her
to call me right away.

51
00:03:29,752 --> 00:03:30,628
Okay…

52
00:03:31,170 --> 00:03:32,504
What is going on?

53
00:03:41,847 --> 00:03:42,973
Patricia.

54
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:47,311
Mom…

55
00:03:49,021 --> 00:03:51,148
I'm so sorry for my reaction.

56
00:03:51,941 --> 00:03:53,400
I know you're surprised.

57
00:03:53,943 --> 00:03:56,403
I still have a lot of questions about him.

58
00:03:57,029 --> 00:04:01,033
His identity, his intentions with you.

59
00:04:01,116 --> 00:04:04,536
Dear, I'm around him every day.

60
00:04:05,621 --> 00:04:08,040
You may doubt him, but…

61
00:04:08,123 --> 00:04:10,501
please don't doubt my judgment.

62
00:04:11,835 --> 00:04:14,088
He has no ill intentions.

63
00:04:14,171 --> 00:04:16,757
I was the one who kept him from leaving.

64
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:21,387
I've never felt this way before, my dear.

65
00:04:22,012 --> 00:04:26,016
The feeling of being loved for who I am.

66
00:04:26,684 --> 00:04:29,019
For having someone stand up for me.

67
00:04:29,645 --> 00:04:32,731
But you can't stop me
from worrying for you.

68
00:04:33,148 --> 00:04:35,943
I thought about all of this
very carefully, dear.

69
00:04:37,027 --> 00:04:40,322
And I made sure that La Familia
is well-protected.

70
00:04:40,406 --> 00:04:41,407
That includes you.

71
00:04:43,158 --> 00:04:44,535
We signed a prenup.

72
00:04:45,369 --> 00:04:47,496
He has no interest in my properties.

73
00:04:47,955 --> 00:04:49,623
So, please, my dear…

74
00:04:50,165 --> 00:04:53,002
I hope you can be happy for me.

75
00:05:00,342 --> 00:05:01,927
Mom, the guest list is at 100 people.

76
00:05:02,011 --> 00:05:03,053
Should I add more?

77
00:05:04,179 --> 00:05:05,639
Can you please? Ugh.

78
00:05:05,723 --> 00:05:07,307
You're pressuring me way too much.

79
00:05:07,391 --> 00:05:09,059
That's your job!

80
00:05:09,143 --> 00:05:10,853
Do it on your own.

81
00:05:15,524 --> 00:05:16,942
Where have you been?

82
00:05:19,528 --> 00:05:20,654
Huh?

83
00:05:21,697 --> 00:05:24,658
We have so many things
to take care of for the wedding.

84
00:05:25,117 --> 00:05:26,744
I'm going to bed.

85
00:05:27,703 --> 00:05:29,204
-Let's talk tomorrow.
-No!

86
00:05:29,288 --> 00:05:31,290
No. I want to talk now.

87
00:05:31,373 --> 00:05:32,791
Let's do it tomorrow.

88
00:05:34,001 --> 00:05:36,045
You went looking for Diana, didn't you?

89
00:05:36,128 --> 00:05:38,047
Why? Were you worried about her?

90
00:05:38,505 --> 00:05:39,715
Jena, April.

91
00:05:40,799 --> 00:05:41,967
Go to your rooms.

92
00:05:50,392 --> 00:05:52,186
We are getting married, Martin!

93
00:05:52,269 --> 00:05:53,937
We're already getting married,

94
00:05:54,021 --> 00:05:56,106
but you still couldn't contain yourself

95
00:05:56,190 --> 00:05:58,442
when you found out that Diana was missing!

96
00:05:59,068 --> 00:06:01,070
Do you think I'm dense?

97
00:06:01,153 --> 00:06:04,948
Tell me the real reason
why you proposed to me!

98
00:06:05,324 --> 00:06:08,911
Is it because Ricardo proposed to Diana?

99
00:06:09,787 --> 00:06:13,123
You couldn't accept
that she already moved on

100
00:06:13,207 --> 00:06:17,086
because you can't stand
seeing her happy without you!

101
00:06:17,169 --> 00:06:19,338
-Huh? What?
-That's enough!

102
00:06:19,421 --> 00:06:20,547
-That's enough, I said!
-Answer me!

103
00:06:20,631 --> 00:06:22,508
Why can't you answer me?

104
00:06:22,841 --> 00:06:24,218
Answer me!

105
00:06:24,718 --> 00:06:25,969
Go on! Do it!

106
00:06:27,554 --> 00:06:29,181
Do it, I dare you!

107
00:06:29,807 --> 00:06:33,018
Am I just here to fill her place?

108
00:06:33,102 --> 00:06:34,603
If that's what you think…

109
00:06:35,395 --> 00:06:37,022
then let's call off the wedding.

110
00:06:37,815 --> 00:06:39,274
No, we can't--

111
00:06:40,109 --> 00:06:41,777
We can't!

112
00:06:42,069 --> 00:06:45,114
Why is it so easy for you to call it off?

113
00:06:45,197 --> 00:06:46,073
Huh?

114
00:06:46,532 --> 00:06:48,325
Tell me, Martin.

115
00:06:48,951 --> 00:06:51,537
Do you still love Diana?

116
00:06:54,790 --> 00:06:55,874
My god…

117
00:06:58,544 --> 00:07:00,921
My whole life!

118
00:07:01,004 --> 00:07:05,175
I gave my whole life to you!

119
00:07:05,259 --> 00:07:08,011
I gave you my whole life!

120
00:07:08,095 --> 00:07:10,722
It's not because of Diana!

121
00:07:11,348 --> 00:07:13,016
It's because of how
you're behaving right now!

122
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:17,271
All you do is compare yourself to Diana.

123
00:07:17,896 --> 00:07:20,190
The one who has a problem here

124
00:07:20,732 --> 00:07:21,942
is you.

125
00:07:25,195 --> 00:07:29,283
Don't turn this around on me.
I'm not blind.

126
00:07:29,867 --> 00:07:31,243
I'm not stupid!

127
00:07:31,910 --> 00:07:34,288
-You want to know the truth?
-What?

128
00:07:34,371 --> 00:07:36,498
I have no face to show…

129
00:07:37,583 --> 00:07:39,042
Patricia…

130
00:07:39,543 --> 00:07:41,461
because of our sins.

131
00:07:41,837 --> 00:07:44,965
I thought we were over this!

132
00:07:45,048 --> 00:07:46,258
That's all in the past!

133
00:07:46,341 --> 00:07:48,468
You know that's not the only thing

134
00:07:48,552 --> 00:07:51,638
we owe Patricia, Carlota.

135
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:53,932
There's more.

136
00:08:01,064 --> 00:08:02,149
Do you know?

137
00:08:02,232 --> 00:08:04,359
To this day, I can't free myself
from the grasp

138
00:08:04,902 --> 00:08:07,905
of the theft that we did in La Familia.

139
00:08:09,656 --> 00:08:10,741
I believe…

140
00:08:11,408 --> 00:08:13,202
the reason I'm leading a miserable life

141
00:08:13,702 --> 00:08:15,162
is because of what we did.

142
00:08:16,413 --> 00:08:18,707
No one else knows that aside from us.

143
00:08:18,790 --> 00:08:21,960
-Sir Lucio knows--
-Sir Lucio is long dead.

144
00:08:22,044 --> 00:08:25,672
He took everything he knew to the grave.

145
00:08:25,756 --> 00:08:29,968
Can't you see that the sins we've done

146
00:08:30,219 --> 00:08:32,387
are all coming out now?

147
00:08:34,598 --> 00:08:36,516
If you want to continue acting
like nothing happened,

148
00:08:37,059 --> 00:08:38,268
I can't do anything about that.

149
00:08:38,644 --> 00:08:43,732
But I can't continue living
like nothing happened.

150
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:45,859
I can't!

151
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:50,948
Martin…

152
00:08:51,031 --> 00:08:52,241
Martin!

153
00:08:53,659 --> 00:08:55,827
Martin, where are you going?

154
00:08:57,371 --> 00:08:58,664
-Like that?
-Mm-hmm.

155
00:08:58,747 --> 00:08:59,998
Add some more.

156
00:09:01,166 --> 00:09:03,460
-Like this?
-Girls, girls.

157
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:06,338
Please set up the dining room.

158
00:09:06,421 --> 00:09:07,839
-Yes, ma'am.
-Okay.

159
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:11,843
I hope Ricardo
and Patricia will like this.

160
00:09:17,724 --> 00:09:19,059
Why, Nanny?

161
00:09:20,644 --> 00:09:22,479
I'm happy for you.

162
00:09:25,649 --> 00:09:28,735
But Patricia didn't seem
to like what happened.

163
00:09:28,819 --> 00:09:30,028
She seemed upset.

164
00:09:30,112 --> 00:09:32,948
When she sees how happy you are,

165
00:09:34,032 --> 00:09:36,493
I'm sure that Patricia
will change her mind.

166
00:09:36,785 --> 00:09:39,705
I'm not going to make
the same mistakes again, Nanny.

167
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:42,916
I will be better.

168
00:09:43,458 --> 00:09:46,044
I will do anything for my family.

169
00:09:54,511 --> 00:09:55,429
Who is it?

170
00:09:56,179 --> 00:09:57,472
It's Uncle Teddy.

171
00:10:00,017 --> 00:10:01,018
Hello, Uncle Teddy.

172
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:02,561
Hello, where are you?

173
00:10:03,395 --> 00:10:04,563
I'm at the mansion.

174
00:10:05,397 --> 00:10:07,149
Is Diana there?

175
00:10:08,066 --> 00:10:10,068
-Yes.
-I'm on my way there.

176
00:10:10,152 --> 00:10:11,862
Do not let her leave.

177
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:13,280
There's something she needs to know.

178
00:10:16,742 --> 00:10:17,743
What did he say?

179
00:10:18,618 --> 00:10:21,371
He said he's coming here
to talk to my mom.

180
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:48,607
It's time, Ricardo.

181
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:51,109
You'll answer to everyone.

182
00:10:51,193 --> 00:10:54,029
I'll expose all of your secrets.

183
00:10:54,112 --> 00:10:57,324
You won't able to set foot
in La Familia again after this.

184
00:11:15,008 --> 00:11:18,178
Your mother's calling for you.
It's time for dinner.

185
00:11:19,221 --> 00:11:20,055
All right.

186
00:11:20,389 --> 00:11:22,766
Okay. By the way, where is Ricardo?

187
00:11:23,558 --> 00:11:24,893
Have you seen him?

188
00:11:24,976 --> 00:11:27,020
-I'll call him myself.
-Okay then.

189
00:11:27,104 --> 00:11:28,313
Go on inside.

190
00:11:28,397 --> 00:11:29,731
-Are you sure?
-Come on, Enzo.

191
00:11:31,024 --> 00:11:31,983
Let's go.

192
00:11:36,196 --> 00:11:37,406
Sir Ricardo?

193
00:11:37,489 --> 00:11:38,782
Sir Ricardo!

194
00:11:44,287 --> 00:11:46,289
Mom's looking for you!

195
00:11:50,252 --> 00:11:51,294
Sis!

196
00:11:56,466 --> 00:11:58,051
Sir Ricardo, Mom's calling for you!

197
00:12:22,284 --> 00:12:23,368
Sir Ricardo?

198
00:12:24,870 --> 00:12:26,329
Oh, Patricia.

199
00:12:26,872 --> 00:12:28,123
Why are you looking for me?

200
00:12:29,916 --> 00:12:30,959
Uh…

201
00:12:33,378 --> 00:12:34,838
What happened to your arm?

202
00:12:36,256 --> 00:12:37,340
Oh, this?

203
00:12:37,883 --> 00:12:38,884
Don't mind it.

204
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:40,927
Dinner's about to start.

205
00:12:42,345 --> 00:12:43,889
Okay. Let's go.

206
00:12:54,441 --> 00:12:56,359
It's our money!

207
00:12:56,443 --> 00:12:58,028
Give us our money back!

208
00:12:58,111 --> 00:13:00,071
-Give us our money!
-What's going on?

209
00:13:00,155 --> 00:13:01,656
They closed the store already!

210
00:13:02,741 --> 00:13:04,451
-Scammers!
-What do you mean?

211
00:13:04,534 --> 00:13:06,286
The Food and Drug Agency shut them down.

212
00:13:06,578 --> 00:13:08,288
A lot of people complained
about their products!

213
00:13:08,371 --> 00:13:10,373
Some had rashes, others had burns.

214
00:13:10,457 --> 00:13:12,083
So, they closed!

215
00:13:12,167 --> 00:13:14,377
They also took the money we invested!

216
00:13:14,461 --> 00:13:16,546
They didn't have
any proper certifications!

217
00:13:16,630 --> 00:13:18,465
All their documents were fake!

218
00:13:20,383 --> 00:13:21,510
Open up!

219
00:13:21,593 --> 00:13:22,469
Come and face me!

220
00:13:22,552 --> 00:13:24,179
Give me back my investment!

221
00:13:30,852 --> 00:13:32,729
April, why are you still up?

222
00:13:34,606 --> 00:13:35,607
Were you crying?

223
00:13:35,690 --> 00:13:38,318
Mom and Dad's wedding got called off.

224
00:13:38,401 --> 00:13:39,694
What happened?

225
00:13:40,904 --> 00:13:42,656
This is your fault!

226
00:13:42,739 --> 00:13:44,366
Wait a minute, please don't hurt her!

227
00:13:44,449 --> 00:13:45,408
Stay out of this.

228
00:13:46,409 --> 00:13:49,162
If it weren't for you and your mother,

229
00:13:49,246 --> 00:13:51,665
Martin wouldn't call off our wedding.

230
00:13:51,748 --> 00:13:54,543
-Mom, calm down!
-Please stop.

231
00:13:54,626 --> 00:13:56,002
Are you happy now?

232
00:13:56,253 --> 00:13:59,214
You are just like your mother.

233
00:14:00,590 --> 00:14:04,135
You ruin everything you touch.

234
00:14:04,553 --> 00:14:05,720
-You're pests!
-Mom! Mom!

235
00:14:05,804 --> 00:14:07,097
That's enough!

236
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:09,349
You have no right to hurt Patricia.

237
00:14:09,933 --> 00:14:12,352
You've finally shown your true colors.

238
00:14:17,399 --> 00:14:19,401
With how long I've been with you…

239
00:14:22,362 --> 00:14:25,156
was how you treated me all just for show?

240
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:28,702
I have been a good daughter to you.

241
00:14:28,785 --> 00:14:31,871
I have never neglected you.

242
00:14:31,955 --> 00:14:35,041
There! That's all you can
hold against me, right?

243
00:14:36,376 --> 00:14:38,128
I'm not holding it against you.

244
00:14:39,671 --> 00:14:40,797
But I was hopeful.

245
00:14:41,172 --> 00:14:42,549
I hoped that one day,

246
00:14:42,632 --> 00:14:45,760
you would also love me
like your own child.

247
00:14:45,844 --> 00:14:49,347
I hoped that you would
at least feel some remorse

248
00:14:49,431 --> 00:14:51,600
for what you have done to our family.

249
00:14:54,311 --> 00:14:57,564
But now you're just proving
that you're really selfish.

250
00:14:57,981 --> 00:14:59,190
Mom!

251
00:14:59,274 --> 00:15:00,900
Mom, that's enough!

252
00:15:00,984 --> 00:15:02,319
Stop it already.

253
00:15:03,695 --> 00:15:04,946
Enough, Mom.

254
00:15:09,367 --> 00:15:12,370
You are ungrateful.

255
00:15:13,455 --> 00:15:15,999
How can I treat you like my child, huh?

256
00:15:16,082 --> 00:15:18,251
Go on, tell me how,

257
00:15:18,335 --> 00:15:24,215
when you remind me every day
of what Diana did to me!

258
00:15:24,758 --> 00:15:26,968
Whatever I do,

259
00:15:27,302 --> 00:15:32,098
your father will always
choose you over us!

260
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:33,975
You know what?

261
00:15:34,601 --> 00:15:36,561
Right from the start…

262
00:15:38,271 --> 00:15:40,899
…I should've returned you
to your mother's womb.

263
00:15:41,316 --> 00:15:43,068
That's what you deserve.

264
00:15:44,235 --> 00:15:45,570
Let's go.

265
00:15:45,654 --> 00:15:47,155
Let's go, Patricia.

266
00:15:47,781 --> 00:15:49,366
-What now?
-Let's go.

267
00:15:51,493 --> 00:15:52,869
Let's head inside, Mom.

268
00:15:57,248 --> 00:15:58,541
Hey, hey, hey.

269
00:16:25,443 --> 00:16:27,487
Hey! I'm not a good dancer.

270
00:16:27,821 --> 00:16:28,947
It's fine.

271
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:41,835
I'm not a good dancer.

272
00:16:42,794 --> 00:16:43,628
See! You're good.

273
00:16:44,254 --> 00:16:45,588
You're taking the lead!

274
00:16:55,682 --> 00:16:57,642
-Happy?
-Yes.

275
00:16:59,144 --> 00:17:02,105
I wish Patricia could accept us.

276
00:17:02,731 --> 00:17:04,357
Do you think she hasn't?

277
00:17:06,109 --> 00:17:08,486
I think she's being forced to accept it.

278
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:13,032
I want us to be a happy family.

279
00:17:16,578 --> 00:17:17,829
I'll take care of it.

280
00:17:19,706 --> 00:17:21,583
I'll convince her.

281
00:17:54,199 --> 00:17:55,408
Dad?

282
00:17:59,245 --> 00:18:00,705
Dad, are you home?

283
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:03,124
Dad?

284
00:18:18,890 --> 00:18:21,518
GEORGIA: DAD, WHERE ARE YOU? ARE YOU OKAY?

285
00:18:47,335 --> 00:18:48,670
YES, GEORGIA. I JUST NEED
SOME TIME TO THINK.

286
00:18:48,753 --> 00:18:49,796
DON'T WORRY. I'LL COME HOME.

287
00:19:29,419 --> 00:19:30,753
-Dad!
-Dad!

288
00:19:35,967 --> 00:19:37,969
Have you been drinking, Dad?

289
00:19:39,095 --> 00:19:40,305
Just a little bit.

290
00:19:41,097 --> 00:19:42,557
What happened?

291
00:19:43,641 --> 00:19:46,603
Mom and Patricia fought.

292
00:19:46,686 --> 00:19:48,980
Mom slapped her.

293
00:19:54,444 --> 00:19:55,862
You hurt my daughter?

294
00:19:57,614 --> 00:19:59,532
Yes, she was disrespecting me.

295
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:03,411
What right do you have to hurt her?

296
00:20:06,456 --> 00:20:08,124
Choose, Martin.

297
00:20:08,958 --> 00:20:13,004
Your family, or your child with Diana.

298
00:20:13,087 --> 00:20:16,341
Don't you dare make me choose!

299
00:20:17,342 --> 00:20:20,762
Oh, my goodness, Martin!
I'm so tired of sharing!

300
00:20:20,845 --> 00:20:23,556
We're complete! We are your family!

301
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:24,766
-Choose!
-No!

302
00:20:24,849 --> 00:20:28,019
We can't lose Patricia!

303
00:20:28,394 --> 00:20:30,021
She's a part of our life!

304
00:20:30,104 --> 00:20:33,524
I also can't lose you! You're all I have!

305
00:20:33,608 --> 00:20:35,151
-I don't care about Patricia!
-I don't care about the rest!

306
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:36,402
-I don't care about Patricia!
-I don't care about the rest!

307
00:20:36,486 --> 00:20:38,571
I can't lose anything anymore!

308
00:20:39,030 --> 00:20:41,616
We can't lose Patricia!

309
00:20:41,699 --> 00:20:43,868
-What is your problem?
-Mom!

310
00:20:45,954 --> 00:20:47,789
-It's all gone!
-What are you saying?

311
00:20:47,872 --> 00:20:49,415
It's all gone! it's all gone!

312
00:20:49,499 --> 00:20:51,918
-It's gone!
-What's gone?

313
00:20:52,293 --> 00:20:53,795
The money!

314
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:55,672
The business!

315
00:20:56,422 --> 00:20:57,298
It's gone.

316
00:20:57,382 --> 00:20:58,716
What?

317
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:01,219
They filed a case against the owner.

318
00:21:01,302 --> 00:21:02,971
The owner's in hiding.

319
00:21:03,054 --> 00:21:04,430
They ran away from me!

320
00:21:04,514 --> 00:21:05,682
They're gone!

321
00:21:07,892 --> 00:21:10,395
They're gone! I don't know what to do!

322
00:22:18,379 --> 00:22:19,380
Enzo.

323
00:22:24,719 --> 00:22:25,887
-Hey.
-Good morning.

324
00:22:25,970 --> 00:22:27,180
Hey.

325
00:22:29,223 --> 00:22:30,308
Morning.

326
00:22:30,933 --> 00:22:33,436
Why are you sleeping here?
You should be in your room.

327
00:22:33,519 --> 00:22:35,605
No, no. I'm fine here.

328
00:22:36,355 --> 00:22:37,482
Besides,

329
00:22:38,733 --> 00:22:42,195
I thought you needed complete rest.

330
00:22:44,530 --> 00:22:46,741
I have a bit of a problem with…

331
00:22:47,283 --> 00:22:48,284
With what?

332
00:22:48,910 --> 00:22:49,911
The…

333
00:22:51,829 --> 00:22:55,083
You're being dramatic!
I don't snore that loudly!

334
00:22:55,166 --> 00:22:56,959
You snore just a bit.

335
00:22:57,668 --> 00:22:59,045
-Are you hungry?
-Mm-hmm.

336
00:22:59,337 --> 00:23:01,005
I'll make breakfast.

337
00:23:05,927 --> 00:23:08,679
Carlota, are you okay?

338
00:23:15,478 --> 00:23:17,563
No, I'm not okay!

339
00:23:18,439 --> 00:23:21,984
The wedding won't happen anymore!

340
00:23:23,027 --> 00:23:26,531
Everything is falling apart!

341
00:23:26,614 --> 00:23:29,617
It's okay. Just let it go. Let it go.

342
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:32,578
I understand it's tough. Just let it go.

343
00:23:58,604 --> 00:24:00,857
Georgia! What's going on? Are you okay?

344
00:24:01,274 --> 00:24:03,401
Patricia, Dad is missing!

345
00:24:03,860 --> 00:24:05,278
-What?
-It's true.

346
00:24:05,361 --> 00:24:08,656
This was his message to me last night.

347
00:24:08,739 --> 00:24:10,908
I tried calling him, but he won't answer.

348
00:24:10,992 --> 00:24:14,120
His phone's been off until now!

349
00:24:14,203 --> 00:24:16,497
He never responded to any messages I sent.

350
00:24:16,581 --> 00:24:19,000
I know something is not right.

351
00:24:19,083 --> 00:24:23,004
He won't do this!
He wouldn't make me worry like this!

352
00:24:23,921 --> 00:24:25,590
-He called me too.
-What?

353
00:24:25,673 --> 00:24:28,426
He said he was going to Mom's
because he has something important to say.

354
00:24:28,509 --> 00:24:30,469
-But he didn't show up.
-What?

355
00:24:30,553 --> 00:24:33,139
Georgia, do you have any idea
what Sir Teddy meant?

356
00:24:33,222 --> 00:24:35,099
No! I have no idea at all!

357
00:24:35,933 --> 00:24:37,059
Calm down.

358
00:24:37,143 --> 00:24:39,228
Think about the last
conversation you had with him.

359
00:24:39,312 --> 00:24:40,271
It might help.

360
00:24:40,813 --> 00:24:42,273
All I know…

361
00:24:42,356 --> 00:24:44,942
is that he became so obsessed
with Sir Ricardo.

362
00:24:47,069 --> 00:24:48,738
He wanted to prove that he was set up.

363
00:25:02,835 --> 00:25:04,170
Miss Cora.

364
00:25:04,587 --> 00:25:05,963
Look at this.

365
00:25:06,339 --> 00:25:07,757
-What's that?
-I wonder what this is.

366
00:25:09,091 --> 00:25:10,134
Is this Ms. D's?

367
00:25:11,385 --> 00:25:13,888
No, this is for men.

368
00:25:24,523 --> 00:25:25,691
Let me go.

369
00:25:27,151 --> 00:25:29,278
Do you think you can get away
with what you've done?

370
00:25:30,571 --> 00:25:32,531
They're already looking for me.

371
00:25:33,032 --> 00:25:34,533
As far as everyone knows,

372
00:25:35,701 --> 00:25:36,827
you're already in hiding.

373
00:25:45,294 --> 00:25:46,504
I was right.

374
00:25:47,421 --> 00:25:49,966
You're the one who ruined me
at La Familia.

375
00:25:51,884 --> 00:25:54,428
We have to make it
look like he's responsible

376
00:25:54,512 --> 00:25:56,555
for Diana's downfall and the company's.

377
00:25:57,765 --> 00:25:58,891
We have to make it look like

378
00:25:58,975 --> 00:26:01,269
Teddy is the only one behind
all the sabotage.

379
00:26:02,395 --> 00:26:03,562
Teddy.

380
00:26:06,482 --> 00:26:08,526
Why are you doing this?

381
00:26:09,485 --> 00:26:10,569
Why?

382
00:26:10,653 --> 00:26:12,822
Why are you taking revenge on us?

383
00:26:13,072 --> 00:26:15,700
Your mother is responsible for everything!

384
00:26:16,033 --> 00:26:17,785
She burned down the factory!

385
00:26:17,868 --> 00:26:19,495
She's a criminal!

386
00:26:23,040 --> 00:26:24,667
My mother did nothing wrong!

387
00:26:24,917 --> 00:26:26,961
Diana covered up the fire!

388
00:26:27,211 --> 00:26:28,921
She put all the blame

389
00:26:29,005 --> 00:26:30,548
on my mother!

390
00:26:33,676 --> 00:26:35,052
Why me?

391
00:26:35,636 --> 00:26:36,595
That was her!

392
00:26:36,679 --> 00:26:39,473
That was Diana,
so why are you coming after me?

393
00:26:39,557 --> 00:26:41,017
Why me?

394
00:26:41,392 --> 00:26:43,477
You already know too much about me, Teddy.

395
00:26:44,770 --> 00:26:47,398
And I won't let you ruin all my plans.

396
00:26:49,317 --> 00:26:51,652
Test that. Electrocute him.

397
00:26:53,195 --> 00:26:54,030
Don't.

398
00:26:56,991 --> 00:26:58,367
Don't.

399
00:26:59,076 --> 00:27:00,536
You're really stubborn.

400
00:27:07,126 --> 00:27:08,461
You're evil.

401
00:27:09,211 --> 00:27:11,380
You're a demon. You're not human.

402
00:27:13,799 --> 00:27:15,593
Why? Are you human?

403
00:27:18,137 --> 00:27:19,388
Is Diana human?

404
00:27:19,805 --> 00:27:21,640
Your shameless father,

405
00:27:21,724 --> 00:27:22,933
Don Lucio…

406
00:27:24,810 --> 00:27:26,062
you Aragons,

407
00:27:26,854 --> 00:27:28,105
are you really human?

408
00:27:34,362 --> 00:27:36,989
Please stop. Stop!

409
00:27:37,323 --> 00:27:39,575
-Teddy, if I let you live…
-Please stop.

410
00:27:39,658 --> 00:27:42,411
-Stop, I can't take it anymore.
-what do I get in return?

411
00:27:43,162 --> 00:27:44,455
Anything. If you want money,

412
00:27:44,538 --> 00:27:46,207
I'll give you as much as you want.

413
00:27:47,083 --> 00:27:49,210
I'll give you any amount you want.

414
00:27:52,338 --> 00:27:54,006
That's nowhere near enough

415
00:27:55,466 --> 00:27:56,967
for my dignity

416
00:27:59,178 --> 00:28:01,097
and my mother's life.

417
00:28:02,306 --> 00:28:03,432
I'll give you anything.

418
00:28:03,724 --> 00:28:06,018
I want all your shares in La Familia.

419
00:28:07,353 --> 00:28:10,439
Why do you want to control La Familia?
My sister won't allow it.

420
00:28:10,523 --> 00:28:11,941
Diana won't allow it.

421
00:28:13,567 --> 00:28:15,319
Diana will follow me.

422
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:17,613
If you value your life,

423
00:28:19,031 --> 00:28:20,574
do as I say.

424
00:28:37,258 --> 00:28:38,551
Ricardo?

425
00:29:04,577 --> 00:29:05,744
Ricardo?

426
00:29:11,542 --> 00:29:12,793
Ricardo?

427
00:30:17,358 --> 00:30:18,901
-Diana.
-Ah.

428
00:30:21,028 --> 00:30:22,321
Ricardo.

429
00:30:22,404 --> 00:30:23,864
You startled me.

430
00:30:24,281 --> 00:30:25,449
What are you doing here?

431
00:30:25,866 --> 00:30:27,117
Um…

432
00:30:27,201 --> 00:30:30,371
I'm looking for its pair
among your things.

433
00:30:30,454 --> 00:30:33,165
The nanny found it at home.

434
00:30:33,249 --> 00:30:34,875
-Mhm.
-You might be looking for it.

435
00:30:35,209 --> 00:30:36,627
How did you get in here?

436
00:30:38,045 --> 00:30:39,880
You have a key in your drawers.

437
00:30:41,340 --> 00:30:43,842
-The key to this place isn't there.
-Yes, I tried.

438
00:30:43,926 --> 00:30:45,177
But it was unlocked.

439
00:30:46,887 --> 00:30:48,347
Is there anyone else here?

440
00:30:52,726 --> 00:30:53,602
No.

441
00:30:56,897 --> 00:30:57,982
It smells like a woman here.

442
00:31:01,151 --> 00:31:02,778
Oh, gosh.

443
00:31:03,362 --> 00:31:04,947
That's my air freshener.

444
00:31:09,326 --> 00:31:11,620
I'll look for its pair myself.

445
00:31:11,912 --> 00:31:13,289
And next time,

446
00:31:13,872 --> 00:31:15,874
don't come here alone.

447
00:31:17,001 --> 00:31:19,670
No, I was just thinking
it might be important to you.

448
00:31:21,505 --> 00:31:23,924
I just want to be the wife you deserve.

449
00:31:24,008 --> 00:31:25,718
I'll take care of you

450
00:31:25,801 --> 00:31:28,137
-the way you take care of me.
-Mm.

451
00:31:29,096 --> 00:31:30,431
I'm really lucky with my wife.

452
00:31:30,514 --> 00:31:31,682
Mm.

453
00:31:55,289 --> 00:31:56,248
Hey, Patricia.

454
00:32:04,256 --> 00:32:07,635
You really have no plans
to apologize to me?

455
00:32:13,891 --> 00:32:18,479
I don't remember anything
I need to apologize to you for.

456
00:32:19,271 --> 00:32:21,231
You're really going to be stubborn.

457
00:32:24,443 --> 00:32:25,903
I don't want to fight, Mom.

458
00:32:27,196 --> 00:32:29,239
Whatever happened between us,

459
00:32:31,408 --> 00:32:33,118
I still respect you.

460
00:32:36,330 --> 00:32:37,873
And I'm tired.

461
00:32:43,962 --> 00:32:46,298
You have some nerve to say you're tired.

462
00:32:46,715 --> 00:32:48,217
Are you tired of our family?

463
00:32:50,260 --> 00:32:51,762
-"Our"?
-Yes.

464
00:32:52,388 --> 00:32:54,932
Didn't you choose your mother?

465
00:32:55,015 --> 00:32:56,975
Fine, then. Just leave us alone.

466
00:32:57,393 --> 00:33:00,688
And let your father fend for himself.

467
00:33:01,230 --> 00:33:02,815
You know, if you're tired,

468
00:33:03,440 --> 00:33:07,319
I'm even more tired of taking on
the problems he gets himself into.

469
00:33:08,946 --> 00:33:11,323
What do you mean? What happened to Dad?

470
00:33:31,218 --> 00:33:33,554
That won't help solve the problem.

471
00:33:39,727 --> 00:33:41,437
Says who?

472
00:33:42,229 --> 00:33:44,189
At least I can somehow forget.

473
00:33:45,983 --> 00:33:47,901
What really happened?

474
00:33:51,780 --> 00:33:53,365
My business.

475
00:33:54,658 --> 00:33:56,118
It turned out to be a scam.

476
00:33:57,411 --> 00:34:00,664
I thought you made sure
it was legal before jumping in.

477
00:34:00,748 --> 00:34:03,500
I made sure. But what can I do?

478
00:34:05,043 --> 00:34:07,713
If a person wants to deceive you,

479
00:34:07,796 --> 00:34:09,840
they will find a way to do it.

480
00:34:10,174 --> 00:34:13,594
Still, you shouldn't have
given your trust that easily.

481
00:34:13,677 --> 00:34:15,804
I didn't get my investment back.

482
00:34:16,722 --> 00:34:19,683
The creditor is already
asking me to pay my debt.

483
00:34:20,976 --> 00:34:22,895
You have savings, right?

484
00:34:24,688 --> 00:34:25,647
Dad.

485
00:34:27,107 --> 00:34:30,027
You've saved some money, right?

486
00:34:31,278 --> 00:34:32,237
Not anymore.

487
00:34:32,988 --> 00:34:34,072
It all went to the car,

488
00:34:34,156 --> 00:34:37,326
the things your mother
and siblings bought,

489
00:34:37,409 --> 00:34:38,994
the preparations for the wedding.

490
00:34:41,205 --> 00:34:42,164
Dear…

491
00:34:43,248 --> 00:34:45,667
I don't know what to do.

492
00:34:47,002 --> 00:34:51,507
I don't know who to turn to for help.

493
00:34:56,386 --> 00:34:57,596
Patricia.

494
00:34:58,347 --> 00:35:01,558
Please help me.
I have no one else to turn to.

495
00:35:02,518 --> 00:35:03,602
Just you.

496
00:35:03,894 --> 00:35:05,103
Please.

497
00:35:13,320 --> 00:35:15,072
I'll help you, Dad.

498
00:35:16,365 --> 00:35:18,242
Thank you, dear.

499
00:35:18,909 --> 00:35:21,161
I know you're the only one I can count on.

500
00:35:22,454 --> 00:35:23,539
Thank you.

501
00:35:32,381 --> 00:35:33,882
I will help you…

502
00:35:35,342 --> 00:35:38,345
…by not giving you any help.

503
00:35:41,557 --> 00:35:45,060
You have to learn
how to deal with your mistakes

504
00:35:45,143 --> 00:35:47,437
without help from anyone,

505
00:35:47,521 --> 00:35:49,022
without help from me.

506
00:35:49,273 --> 00:35:50,399
Patricia.

507
00:35:53,902 --> 00:35:55,529
You need this, Dad.

508
00:35:55,904 --> 00:35:58,448
This is not the first time
this has happened.

509
00:36:00,617 --> 00:36:04,121
This is the only way
you can correct all your mistakes.

510
00:36:06,498 --> 00:36:08,208
I love you so much, Dad.

511
00:36:11,920 --> 00:36:14,006
This isn't easy for me.

512
00:36:16,884 --> 00:36:19,177
This is the only solution I can see.

513
00:36:49,333 --> 00:36:51,543
The medicine worked. Let's meet.

514
00:36:56,131 --> 00:36:57,424
Ricardo.

515
00:36:59,384 --> 00:37:00,469
Oh, Nanny.

516
00:37:02,262 --> 00:37:04,139
You're leaving?

517
00:37:04,222 --> 00:37:06,808
Yes. I need to get my things
from my house.

518
00:37:07,893 --> 00:37:09,645
Why don't you just do it tomorrow?

519
00:37:09,728 --> 00:37:10,729
It's already late.

520
00:37:10,812 --> 00:37:13,398
I want to spend all day
tomorrow with Diana.

521
00:37:14,983 --> 00:37:16,735
Where's Diana?

522
00:37:17,527 --> 00:37:18,487
She's already sleeping.

523
00:37:19,488 --> 00:37:20,697
An early night for her, huh?

524
00:37:21,698 --> 00:37:24,284
Diana made the right choice with you.

525
00:37:25,786 --> 00:37:27,412
How come?

526
00:37:27,496 --> 00:37:29,373
She has a hard time sleeping at night.

527
00:37:29,456 --> 00:37:33,377
She's always thinking about work,
about her problems.

528
00:37:33,794 --> 00:37:34,878
But…

529
00:37:35,671 --> 00:37:38,507
You're the only one
who can put her at ease.

530
00:37:40,342 --> 00:37:41,385
Well…

531
00:37:41,885 --> 00:37:46,515
…I promised myself that
I'll take care of Diana.

532
00:37:48,058 --> 00:37:49,851
Go on, get some rest now. It's late.

533
00:37:49,935 --> 00:37:52,562
-Okay. Take care.
-Okay.

534
00:37:59,569 --> 00:38:02,030
Do you have any leads
as to where your father is?

535
00:38:02,114 --> 00:38:03,907
I already filed a police report.

536
00:38:04,866 --> 00:38:06,660
But they said that
Dad is already an adult.

537
00:38:07,911 --> 00:38:10,455
And he also replied that he's okay.

538
00:38:10,539 --> 00:38:13,166
So, they cannot consider him missing.

539
00:38:14,501 --> 00:38:16,294
But I feel like something's wrong.

540
00:38:17,421 --> 00:38:19,631
I'm just starting to feel helpless.

541
00:38:20,632 --> 00:38:23,552
If we have any idea where to start…

542
00:38:25,345 --> 00:38:26,888
we can look for him ourselves.

543
00:38:28,974 --> 00:38:30,183
There is.

544
00:38:30,267 --> 00:38:32,436
Somewhere he is supposed to go.

545
00:38:35,230 --> 00:38:36,606
There. Him.

546
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:44,072
His car has a dashcam, Patricia.

547
00:38:48,368 --> 00:38:49,911
Uhm, excuse me.

548
00:38:49,995 --> 00:38:51,663
Are you always parked here?

549
00:38:51,747 --> 00:38:52,664
Yes, why?

550
00:39:02,841 --> 00:39:04,968
Sir Teddy did come here.

551
00:39:05,802 --> 00:39:07,596
What I don't understand is,

552
00:39:08,346 --> 00:39:09,806
he told me on the phone

553
00:39:09,890 --> 00:39:12,726
there's something important
that he'd like Mom to know.

554
00:39:14,478 --> 00:39:15,979
Why didn't he go inside?

555
00:39:16,563 --> 00:39:17,898
Why did he leave?

556
00:39:23,070 --> 00:39:25,447
-Congratulations, sir.
-Thank you.

557
00:39:26,073 --> 00:39:28,075
-Congratulations, sir.
-Thank you.

558
00:39:30,410 --> 00:39:32,162
Hello, sir, we heard the news.

559
00:39:32,245 --> 00:39:34,039
Congratulations to you and Ms. D.

560
00:39:34,122 --> 00:39:35,874
We're all very happy for you, sir.

561
00:39:35,957 --> 00:39:37,334
Thank you. Thank you, guys.

562
00:39:37,751 --> 00:39:39,419
-Congratulations, sir.
-Thank you.

563
00:39:39,711 --> 00:39:41,755
Hi, Ricardo. I heard you're back.

564
00:39:41,838 --> 00:39:44,841
I saw the reinstatement papers
that Diana sent.

565
00:39:45,092 --> 00:39:48,011
And congratulations to the both of you!

566
00:39:48,095 --> 00:39:49,304
-Thank you.
-Nico?

567
00:39:49,387 --> 00:39:52,015
-Sir, congratulations.
-Oh.

568
00:39:53,058 --> 00:39:54,059
That's for you.

569
00:39:55,185 --> 00:39:56,520
Oh, wow.

570
00:39:56,603 --> 00:39:59,731
Remember, I am the first
board member to give a gift.

571
00:40:00,649 --> 00:40:02,150
What is this? A gift or a bribe?

572
00:40:03,318 --> 00:40:05,112
I'm just kidding, Ms. Angeles.

573
00:40:05,195 --> 00:40:06,488
We'll be working together for a long time.

574
00:40:06,863 --> 00:40:07,906
Why is that?

575
00:40:07,989 --> 00:40:10,158
Well, since Diana's on leave,

576
00:40:10,242 --> 00:40:12,452
she instructed me to attend the meetings.

577
00:40:12,786 --> 00:40:14,496
I'll be her eyes and ears here.

578
00:40:14,788 --> 00:40:16,081
I'm looking forward to that.

579
00:40:16,414 --> 00:40:18,875
Yes, me too. I need someone I can trust.

580
00:40:29,970 --> 00:40:32,180
-Take care of that, okay?
-Thank you. Thank you.

581
00:40:33,515 --> 00:40:34,641
Martin!

582
00:40:35,433 --> 00:40:37,811
-It's Martin!
-Go back, bro.

583
00:40:40,147 --> 00:40:41,273
Hey! Martin!

584
00:40:42,899 --> 00:40:44,151
I already paid for this!

585
00:40:44,943 --> 00:40:48,029
-Martin!
-Get out, Martin! Get out!

586
00:40:48,113 --> 00:40:49,114
Out of the car!

587
00:40:49,698 --> 00:40:51,116
Trying to ditch us, huh?

588
00:40:51,199 --> 00:40:52,450
Bring him here.

589
00:40:52,534 --> 00:40:53,702
-Where are you going?
-Quick!

590
00:40:55,162 --> 00:40:57,205
-Trying to run away, huh?
-Come here!

591
00:40:57,914 --> 00:40:59,457
All debt needs to be paid!

592
00:40:59,541 --> 00:41:00,750
The boss has been looking
for the money for so long!

593
00:41:00,834 --> 00:41:02,043
Is that money? Give me that!

594
00:41:02,127 --> 00:41:03,587
-No, no, no!
-Let go!

595
00:41:03,670 --> 00:41:04,754
-No, no!
-You don't want to let go?

596
00:41:07,382 --> 00:41:08,466
Let's go!

597
00:41:11,553 --> 00:41:14,055
Hey! Hey!

598
00:41:21,438 --> 00:41:22,564
Carlota.

599
00:41:22,647 --> 00:41:26,443
Ah! Uh, sir, what can I do for you?

600
00:41:26,526 --> 00:41:30,822
I have a meeting in San Vicente
and no idea how to get there.

601
00:41:30,906 --> 00:41:33,658
So, since my secretary is away on leave,

602
00:41:33,742 --> 00:41:34,993
I need you to accompany me.

603
00:41:35,076 --> 00:41:37,579
Sure, sir. But what about Mr. Borja?

604
00:41:37,662 --> 00:41:40,540
I've already told Mr. Borja
I'm borrowing you for the day.

605
00:41:41,166 --> 00:41:42,876
If that's okay with you.

606
00:41:43,835 --> 00:41:44,920
It's okay.

607
00:41:46,463 --> 00:41:48,548
-Sure, sir.
-Good.

608
00:41:50,675 --> 00:41:52,427
He's missing?

609
00:41:53,762 --> 00:41:55,055
Yes, Ms. D.

610
00:41:55,138 --> 00:41:58,391
Georgia told us that
Sir Teddy hasn't come home.

611
00:41:58,475 --> 00:42:00,518
We reported it to the police too, Ms. D.

612
00:42:00,602 --> 00:42:03,313
But since Georgia received
a text from Sir Teddy,

613
00:42:03,396 --> 00:42:05,982
he can't be considered
a missing person yet.

614
00:42:06,650 --> 00:42:08,443
The night we had dinner here,

615
00:42:08,526 --> 00:42:09,819
I talked to Uncle Teddy.

616
00:42:09,903 --> 00:42:12,697
He said he'd come over,
but he never made it.

617
00:42:13,657 --> 00:42:15,575
Patricia, he didn't make it.

618
00:42:17,077 --> 00:42:18,495
Why look for him here?

619
00:42:18,787 --> 00:42:21,706
The night he disappeared,
I saw you outside.

620
00:42:24,501 --> 00:42:26,628
Patricia, what are you trying to imply?

621
00:42:27,379 --> 00:42:29,256
I didn't say anything.

622
00:42:29,339 --> 00:42:32,259
You say nothing, yet you're accusing me.

623
00:42:32,342 --> 00:42:35,095
What do you think I'd do to Teddy?

624
00:42:35,178 --> 00:42:37,681
I want Teddy out of hiding

625
00:42:37,764 --> 00:42:40,058
so he can pay for his sins
against La Familia.

626
00:42:40,141 --> 00:42:42,060
Wait, hold on. Hold on.

627
00:42:42,894 --> 00:42:44,479
We don't need to fight about this.

628
00:42:44,562 --> 00:42:46,731
We need to find Teddy.

629
00:42:46,815 --> 00:42:48,108
What should we do?

630
00:42:48,191 --> 00:42:49,818
Ms. D, we can clear this up

631
00:42:49,901 --> 00:42:52,737
if we see the CCTV footage
from the gate of the mansion.

632
00:42:52,821 --> 00:42:54,739
-That's right.
-Nanny?

633
00:42:54,823 --> 00:42:55,657
Yes, ma'am?

634
00:42:55,740 --> 00:42:57,701
Nanny, get my tablet, please.

635
00:42:57,784 --> 00:42:59,494
Yes, ma'am. Right away.

636
00:43:00,078 --> 00:43:02,414
Where is Teddy? What--

637
00:43:08,545 --> 00:43:10,672
Okay, here. Let's…

638
00:43:11,798 --> 00:43:12,799
Oh.

639
00:43:21,057 --> 00:43:23,476
Wait, what--

640
00:43:23,560 --> 00:43:25,228
-May I, Ms. D?
-What happened?

641
00:43:26,313 --> 00:43:27,564
Why did it cut out?

642
00:43:35,280 --> 00:43:38,074
Looks like the system was offline
from seven p.m. to nine p.m.

643
00:43:38,408 --> 00:43:39,826
-What?
-Yes, Ms. D.

644
00:43:39,909 --> 00:43:42,245
This happens during power outages.

645
00:43:42,329 --> 00:43:44,164
Wait, there wasn't a power outage,
was there?

646
00:43:45,206 --> 00:43:46,249
Right?

647
00:43:48,251 --> 00:43:50,128
-Are you sure?
-How convenient.

648
00:43:51,838 --> 00:43:53,340
I'll call my contacts,

649
00:43:53,715 --> 00:43:56,217
maybe they can help us search for Teddy.

650
00:44:01,014 --> 00:44:02,349
It's a good thing you came along with me.

651
00:44:02,432 --> 00:44:03,892
Traffic is horrible.

652
00:44:04,517 --> 00:44:06,394
Where is your driver, sir?

653
00:44:06,478 --> 00:44:09,397
Oh, no. I like… I like driving.

654
00:44:09,481 --> 00:44:11,941
-Mm-hmm.
-I just didn't expect it to be so bad.

655
00:44:12,525 --> 00:44:15,236
Yes. Well, I can entertain you, sir.

656
00:44:15,320 --> 00:44:17,572
-Okay.
-I can sing.

657
00:44:17,655 --> 00:44:20,367
I can tell you stories.

658
00:44:20,450 --> 00:44:22,827
-That's good.
-Do you like any…

659
00:44:22,911 --> 00:44:25,121
Are you okay, sir?

660
00:44:25,372 --> 00:44:26,331
Sir?

661
00:44:26,414 --> 00:44:27,707
Sir? Sir?

662
00:44:27,791 --> 00:44:30,668
Oh god, we're going to crash! Sir!

663
00:44:30,752 --> 00:44:33,463
Sir, wake up! Sir, sir, sir!

664
00:44:33,546 --> 00:44:34,756
Sir…

665
00:44:41,971 --> 00:44:43,473
The patient is doing fine now.

666
00:44:43,556 --> 00:44:45,016
He suddenly passed out

667
00:44:45,100 --> 00:44:46,976
due to a sudden drop
in his blood pressure.

668
00:44:47,352 --> 00:44:48,561
We managed to treat it in time.

669
00:44:48,853 --> 00:44:52,816
He just has a sprained foot
from the impact of the crash.

670
00:44:52,899 --> 00:44:55,318
He's doing fine.
He's under observation for now.

671
00:44:55,402 --> 00:44:58,696
Your MRI results came back clear.

672
00:44:59,072 --> 00:45:02,617
Negative for internal bleeding
and fractures.

673
00:45:03,076 --> 00:45:04,244
Thank you, doc.

674
00:45:04,327 --> 00:45:06,996
-Please stay here for now.
-Thank you, doc.

675
00:45:14,212 --> 00:45:16,714
How are you feeling, sir?

676
00:45:19,217 --> 00:45:20,301
You saved my life.

677
00:45:20,385 --> 00:45:24,931
What's important is that
you're okay and safe.

678
00:45:25,223 --> 00:45:28,143
I owe my life to you, Carlota.

679
00:45:28,226 --> 00:45:32,147
-Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom!
-Mom! Mom, we're here now.

680
00:45:32,230 --> 00:45:33,731
-Oh…
-Mom, are you okay?

681
00:45:33,815 --> 00:45:36,192
We thought we were going to lose you.

682
00:45:36,276 --> 00:45:38,027
-Shh! Zip it.
-What?

683
00:45:39,320 --> 00:45:43,158
I'm fine.
I wouldn't just leave you guys like that.

684
00:45:43,241 --> 00:45:48,955
I still have to care for you
and take responsibility.

685
00:45:51,875 --> 00:45:53,168
Uh…

686
00:45:53,626 --> 00:45:54,836
April, Jena,

687
00:45:54,919 --> 00:45:57,505
this is my boss, Mr. Smith.

688
00:45:57,589 --> 00:46:03,845
Mr. Smith, these are my children,
April and Jena.

689
00:46:04,345 --> 00:46:05,763
She saved my life.

690
00:46:09,976 --> 00:46:13,480
Mom, what about the hospital bill?
How do we pay?

691
00:46:14,981 --> 00:46:19,986
Don't worry,
my boss is someone we can count on.

692
00:46:20,320 --> 00:46:23,823
He paid for my hospital bill.

693
00:46:24,949 --> 00:46:27,410
He covered everything.

694
00:46:30,497 --> 00:46:34,834
I have a job for you,
and I know you can handle it.

695
00:46:35,627 --> 00:46:36,503
What is it?

696
00:46:36,586 --> 00:46:38,963
It's a bit sensitive, but…

697
00:46:42,175 --> 00:46:43,676
you won't regret it.

698
00:46:47,805 --> 00:46:48,640
Sir?

699
00:46:48,723 --> 00:46:53,770
Just transfer the company assets
to the new accounts I'm giving you.

700
00:46:57,023 --> 00:47:01,444
Sir, it's not easy to move company assets
to new accounts.

701
00:47:01,528 --> 00:47:03,988
And I might get caught.

702
00:47:04,072 --> 00:47:05,823
I'll protect you.

703
00:47:06,741 --> 00:47:09,244
-I'll handle it.
-But, sir…

704
00:47:09,327 --> 00:47:11,162
if we do this,

705
00:47:11,246 --> 00:47:14,457
we'll lose a huge chunk
of our operating funds.

706
00:47:14,541 --> 00:47:16,501
The company will become an empty shell.

707
00:47:16,584 --> 00:47:17,919
I know.

708
00:47:19,629 --> 00:47:21,130
If you don't want to…

709
00:47:22,632 --> 00:47:23,841
Sir…

710
00:47:25,802 --> 00:47:27,095
Well?

711
00:47:30,598 --> 00:47:32,308
Fine, I'll do it.

712
00:47:41,025 --> 00:47:42,151
-Sir?
-Yes, what is it?

713
00:47:42,235 --> 00:47:44,487
Someone's looking for Sir Teddy.

714
00:47:44,571 --> 00:47:46,364
He said he's his private investigator.

715
00:49:11,741 --> 00:49:13,159
Where do you think you're going?

716
00:49:37,350 --> 00:49:39,102
Where is the investigator?

717
00:49:40,603 --> 00:49:43,564
Where is the investigator?
They said he was right here.

718
00:49:47,944 --> 00:49:49,195
Where is Sir Teddy?

719
00:49:53,241 --> 00:49:54,951
Are you Mr. Silva?

720
00:49:55,034 --> 00:49:56,494
Yes, that's me.

721
00:49:56,577 --> 00:49:58,830
I'm here to collect payment
from Sir Teddy.

722
00:49:58,913 --> 00:50:00,832
He hasn't paid me yet.

723
00:50:01,541 --> 00:50:03,209
He's missing.

724
00:50:03,292 --> 00:50:06,212
And we suspect something bad
has happened to him.

725
00:50:06,295 --> 00:50:09,924
Did something bad really happen,
or is he just avoiding me?

726
00:50:10,466 --> 00:50:13,803
-Hey, my dad is not a scammer!
-Georgia. Georgia, calm down.

727
00:50:13,886 --> 00:50:17,014
Sir, he asked you
to investigate something, correct?

728
00:50:17,098 --> 00:50:19,726
Did you find out anything about it?

729
00:50:20,143 --> 00:50:21,769
About Ricardo Salvador?

730
00:50:21,853 --> 00:50:25,773
First of all, you're asking
about client information.

731
00:50:26,232 --> 00:50:27,650
I can't share that with anyone.

732
00:50:28,693 --> 00:50:31,362
Second, I don't have anything to tell you,

733
00:50:31,446 --> 00:50:33,197
because I didn't find anything.

734
00:50:33,281 --> 00:50:37,034
I spoke with Uncle Teddy.
He said he found out a lot.

735
00:50:37,118 --> 00:50:38,453
Didn't that information come from you?

736
00:50:38,953 --> 00:50:42,290
Dad also mentioned he's been
in constant contact with you.

737
00:50:42,582 --> 00:50:43,916
Did you learn anything?

738
00:50:44,584 --> 00:50:48,629
I won't say anything
because I haven't been paid.

739
00:50:48,713 --> 00:50:51,382
Now, if Sir Teddy really isn't here,

740
00:50:51,466 --> 00:50:53,801
please tell him to transfer his payment.

741
00:50:54,135 --> 00:50:56,971
-Hey--No, hey!
-Georgia.

742
00:50:57,597 --> 00:50:58,639
Let's go.

743
00:50:59,849 --> 00:51:01,058
Come on.

744
00:51:25,917 --> 00:51:26,793
Why the look?

745
00:51:28,419 --> 00:51:29,837
Did you enjoy the dinner?

746
00:51:31,756 --> 00:51:35,051
I don't want you worrying
about other problems here, Diana.

747
00:51:36,803 --> 00:51:37,720
Here.

748
00:51:38,638 --> 00:51:40,181
To help you relax.

749
00:51:43,851 --> 00:51:46,854
Even if I wanted to,
I can't force myself to relax.

750
00:51:46,938 --> 00:51:47,772
Why?

751
00:51:48,564 --> 00:51:49,524
Teddy's missing.

752
00:51:54,570 --> 00:51:55,696
Diana…

753
00:51:55,780 --> 00:51:58,866
Being missing is different
from hiding, okay?

754
00:51:59,826 --> 00:52:02,703
Don't worry.
I already hired someone to find him.

755
00:52:02,787 --> 00:52:04,038
And I promise you,

756
00:52:04,121 --> 00:52:05,957
by the time we return from our honeymoon,

757
00:52:06,040 --> 00:52:07,542
everything will be sorted out.

758
00:52:08,292 --> 00:52:09,544
Okay?

759
00:52:09,627 --> 00:52:11,629
Go on. Take the pill.

760
00:52:35,278 --> 00:52:37,572
-Sorry, I have to take this.
-Diana.

761
00:52:37,655 --> 00:52:39,323
This will be quick.

762
00:52:39,407 --> 00:52:41,784
This will be the last
for our whole trip, I promise.

763
00:52:43,077 --> 00:52:44,245
Okay.

764
00:53:15,109 --> 00:53:17,111
What's the update on the thing
I asked you to do?

765
00:53:17,194 --> 00:53:20,406
Ma'am, be careful around Ricardo Salvador.

766
00:53:20,781 --> 00:53:24,619
He's been talking to one
of La Familia's accountants.

767
00:53:24,702 --> 00:53:27,830
Looks like they're scheming
to steal company assets.

768
00:53:28,831 --> 00:53:30,708
What else did you find out?

769
00:53:30,791 --> 00:53:33,252
He's frequently meeting a woman.

770
00:53:33,336 --> 00:53:34,587
What's her name?

771
00:53:35,671 --> 00:53:36,797
Sandra.

772
00:53:43,971 --> 00:53:45,598
I need you to do something.

773
00:53:46,265 --> 00:53:48,643
Find out what happened to my brother.

774
00:53:48,726 --> 00:53:50,186
And tail Ricardo.

775
00:53:50,478 --> 00:53:52,104
Find out his every move.

776
00:53:52,188 --> 00:53:54,315
Be careful. He can't know about this.

777
00:53:54,398 --> 00:53:55,483
Yes, ma'am.

778
00:53:59,403 --> 00:54:02,406
The pill he keeps giving me,
do you know what it is?

779
00:54:02,823 --> 00:54:03,824
Yes, ma'am.

780
00:54:03,908 --> 00:54:06,202
Doctors don't just simply prescribe it.

781
00:54:06,285 --> 00:54:08,371
And it shouldn't be taken for long periods

782
00:54:08,454 --> 00:54:11,123
because it's highly addictive.

783
00:54:11,207 --> 00:54:15,294
Frequent consumption may cause confusion

784
00:54:15,378 --> 00:54:18,798
that could lead to memory loss.

785
00:54:18,881 --> 00:54:21,884
You may also lose control of your body.

786
00:54:21,968 --> 00:54:24,887
I'm still finding out why
Ricardo is doing this.

787
00:54:25,388 --> 00:54:28,265
Okay. Let's just talk
when you have updates.

788
00:54:28,349 --> 00:54:29,642
Okay.

789
00:54:37,775 --> 00:54:38,901
Who is this?

790
00:54:39,652 --> 00:54:41,779
Sis, it's Teddy.

791
00:54:41,862 --> 00:54:44,657
Teddy? Teddy, oh, my god. Where are you?

792
00:54:44,740 --> 00:54:46,075
What happened to you?

793
00:54:47,451 --> 00:54:48,744
Diana, listen to me.

794
00:54:48,828 --> 00:54:51,122
Stay away from Ricardo. He's dangerous.

795
00:54:51,205 --> 00:54:52,540
Yes, I know that now,

796
00:54:52,623 --> 00:54:55,459
but I don't understand
why he's doing this.

797
00:54:55,543 --> 00:54:57,795
Why is he doing this to us?

798
00:54:57,878 --> 00:55:00,631
He infiltrated La Familia
to take over the company.

799
00:55:00,715 --> 00:55:03,050
He wants us to suffer, especially you.

800
00:55:03,134 --> 00:55:05,594
-He's taking revenge.
-Revenge?

801
00:55:05,678 --> 00:55:07,555
What did we ever do to him?

802
00:55:08,139 --> 00:55:12,351
Ricardo is the son of Cecilia Pineda.

803
00:55:12,435 --> 00:55:13,894
He hid his real identity.

804
00:55:13,978 --> 00:55:16,731
Everything he told you was made up.
They were all lies!

805
00:55:16,814 --> 00:55:19,316
He wants us to pay
for what happened to his mother.

806
00:55:19,400 --> 00:55:21,485
If I were you, I'd leave while I can.

807
00:55:21,569 --> 00:55:23,195
You're not safe. Get out of there!

808
00:55:23,279 --> 00:55:24,321
Go now, Diana!

809
00:55:26,198 --> 00:55:27,992
Hello? Hello?

810
00:55:28,075 --> 00:55:28,909
Teddy?

811
00:55:31,620 --> 00:55:32,747
Hello?

812
00:56:14,038 --> 00:56:14,914
Diana!

813
00:56:21,128 --> 00:56:22,004
Ah!

814
00:56:27,676 --> 00:56:29,261
Don't come near me!

815
00:56:29,345 --> 00:56:30,346
Don't come near me!

816
00:56:36,560 --> 00:56:38,270
How could you do this to me?

817
00:56:38,354 --> 00:56:40,356
You said you would take care of me!

818
00:56:40,439 --> 00:56:41,857
You said you loved me!

819
00:56:41,941 --> 00:56:43,734
Turns out they were all lies!

820
00:56:43,818 --> 00:56:45,319
How could you do this?

821
00:56:45,945 --> 00:56:48,531
This isn't supposed to happen so soon,

822
00:56:48,614 --> 00:56:50,699
but you just had to expedite my plans.

823
00:56:50,783 --> 00:56:52,785
I wanted to enjoy our marriage longer.

824
00:57:07,550 --> 00:57:08,759
Don't worry.

825
00:57:09,969 --> 00:57:11,929
I'll get to your daughter next.

826
00:57:12,721 --> 00:57:16,684
Don't hurt my daughter! Don't you dare!

827
00:57:17,017 --> 00:57:19,770
The pain I made you feel…

828
00:57:20,521 --> 00:57:23,190
isn't enough to compensate
for my mother's death!

829
00:57:23,274 --> 00:57:24,733
Agh! Ah!

830
00:57:54,847 --> 00:57:55,848
Ugh!

831
00:58:32,092 --> 00:58:34,053
What happened? How did Mom go missing?

832
00:58:34,136 --> 00:58:35,095
Is it true…

833
00:58:35,179 --> 00:58:37,431
that you were the only one
she was with in the rest house?

834
00:58:37,514 --> 00:58:38,974
We were the only ones in the rest house.

835
00:58:39,058 --> 00:58:40,392
I won't fall for your act.

836
00:58:40,476 --> 00:58:43,062
I will make sure you don't succeed!

837
00:58:43,145 --> 00:58:45,356
Let's work together to save La Familia.

838
00:58:45,439 --> 00:58:46,565
Save or destroy?

839
00:58:46,649 --> 00:58:48,609
There's a lot you don't know
about what happened.

840
00:58:48,692 --> 00:58:50,444
Did you lie to me, Patricia?

841
00:58:50,527 --> 00:58:54,531
If Diana were here now,
she'd want us to carry on.

842
00:58:54,615 --> 00:58:55,491
Liar!

843
00:58:55,574 --> 00:58:59,119
I won't let you carry on
until you return my mother!
